            "body": "**Codex bot review · model: `gpt-6-astra`**\n\nReviewed `32ea4058a342` against base `a0f7b9f4e8e3`.\n\nThank you for your contribution! No actionable findings. Both test modules now use the same device predicate as their APIs. The shared NSA setup and selection/SWA coverage remain unchanged.\n\nValidation: The native SM100 NSA L0 suite completed with 33 passed, 2 skipped and 1 deselected using CuTe DSL 4.8.0. Twenty-three modeled host checks passed: both helpers across seven capability values, all four test entry points skipping before plan setup on cc 12.0 and continuing on cc 10.0, and shared NSA setup remaining accessible on cc 12.0. Precheck found no candidates.\n\nLimitations: No native cc 12.x device was available. Its new skip paths were checked with modeled capability, without launching a kernel under that model. The covering python/misc CI route remains on access hold. Style and Security workflows require maintainer approval.\n\nApproved: no P0 or high-risk P1 found. Remaining findings stay with the owner; merge timing stays with the owner.\n\n<!-- codex-fe-review:v2:2237:32ea4058a342850e4f6285968b57a07e758c5b7d:complete:no-blocker -->",
